{
 "id": "def-galois-scheme-descent-data-category",
 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Category of scheme descent data",
 "statement": "Let S and X be schemes [def-pc-scheme] and a:X→S a morphism. The category DD(a) has objects pairs (V,D), where V is a scheme over X and D is a transport descent datum [def-pd-descent-datum]. A morphism from (V,D) to (W,E) is a morphism α:V→W over X for which E(f₀,f₁)(zα)=D(f₀,f₁)(z)α for every test scheme, pair f₀,f₁ with equal composites to S, and point z of V over f₀. Composition and identity are those of the over category.",
 "source": {
